<item>
  <title>Setting up this site</title>
  <dc:creator>Abhishek Bhattacharjee</dc:creator>
  <link>https://stat-absk.github.io/posts/welcome/</link>
  <description><![CDATA[ 





<p>This site is a <a href="https://quarto.org">Quarto</a> website, edited in RStudio and hosted on GitHub Pages. The whole thing is plain text — <code>.qmd</code> files plus one YAML config — which means it versions cleanly in git and anything I can compute in R can go straight into a page.</p>
<section id="adding-a-post" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="adding-a-post">Adding a post</h2>
<p>Each post is a folder under <code>posts/</code> containing an <code>index.qmd</code>:</p>
<pre><code>posts/
  welcome/index.qmd
  my-new-post/
    index.qmd
    a-figure.png</code></pre>
<p>The folder-per-post layout keeps images next to the text that uses them, and the published URL comes out as <code>/posts/my-new-post/</code>.</p>
<p>The front matter needs four things:</p>
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode" id="cb2" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode yaml code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode yaml"><span id="cb2-1"><span class="pp" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">---</span></span>
<span id="cb2-2"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">title</span><span class="kw" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-weight: bold;
font-style: inherit;">:</span><span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"> </span><span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"The title"</span></span>
<span id="cb2-3"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">description</span><span class="kw" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-weight: bold;
font-style: inherit;">:</span><span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"> </span><span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"One line that shows up on the blog listing."</span></span>
<span id="cb2-4"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">date</span><span class="kw" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-weight: bold;
font-style: inherit;">:</span><span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"> 2026-09-01</span></span>
<span id="cb2-5"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">categories</span><span class="kw" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-weight: bold;
font-style: inherit;">:</span><span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"> </span><span class="kw" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-weight: bold;
font-style: inherit;">[</span><span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">rstats</span><span class="kw" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-weight: bold;
font-style: inherit;">,</span><span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"> notes</span><span class="kw" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-weight: bold;
font-style: inherit;">]</span></span>
<span id="cb2-6"><span class="pp" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">---</span></span></code></pre></div></div>
<p>Then <strong>Render</strong> in RStudio, and the post appears on the <a href="../../blog.html">blog page</a> automatically — the listing reads the <code>posts/</code> folder, so there’s no index to update by hand.</p>
</section>
<section id="why-quarto-over-r-markdown" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="why-quarto-over-r-markdown">Why Quarto over R Markdown</h2>
<p>Mostly that the website machinery is built in rather than bolted on, that <code>freeze: auto</code> means old posts don’t re-run their code on every build, and that the same <code>.qmd</code> can render to HTML, PDF, or slides without changing the source.</p>


