<p>Each extra 1000 lb costs roughly 3.2 mpg, holding cylinder count fixed. That number isn’t typed in — it’s an <em>inline</em> R expression, written like this:</p>
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode" id="cb5" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode markdown code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode markdown"><span id="cb5-1">Each extra 1000 lb costs roughly 3.2 mpg.</span></code></pre></div></div>
<p>(In a <code>.qmd</code> the inline form is a backtick span starting with <code>r</code>.) Refit the model and the sentence updates itself, so the prose can never drift away from the numbers.</p>
